From 571b9b76a7aec5c615d0c456a331fff5b0d0801b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RivonClaw CI <ci@rivonclaw.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 04:51:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(openclaw): recover invalid prepared model catalog
 generations

Why:
- Full models.list discovery can retain a worker whose reconstructed plugin/runtime fingerprint no longer matches the published configured owner.
- Subsequent Feishu dispatches then reuse the poisoned generation and fail before an agent run starts.
- Backports OpenClaw PR #126224 / issue #126108 at head 059bea02f804144e33e169f90267d365b4d6a490 (commits ff86038a632, 032f51cb5e0, 059bea02f80), adapted to the pinned source layout.

Removal:
- Drop this patch when .openclaw-version contains merged OpenClaw PR #126224 at 059bea02f804144e33e169f90267d365b4d6a490 or an equivalent successor that replaces configured owners after catalog generation mismatch and gates concurrent recovery readers.

Tests:
- src/agents/prepared-model-catalog-worker.integration.test.ts
- apps/desktop/src/gateway/vendor-prepared-model-catalog-recovery.sentinel.test.ts
